  "wikitext": "{{Short description|Red alga}}\n{{one source|date=September 2025}}\n{{Speciesbox\n| genus = Porphyra\n| species = linearis\n| authority = Greville\n}}\n\n'''''Porphyra linearis''''' is a [[red alga]] found in the coastal waters of [[Japan]]. It has only four chromosomes (2n=4)<ref>{{cite journal | last= Dangeard | first= Pierre | date= June 1927 | title= Recherches sur les Bangia et les Porphyra | journal= Le Botaniste |url=https://archive.org/details/le-botaniste_1926-1927_0/page/223/mode/1up?view=theater | volume= 18 | issue= 5 | page= 223 }}</ref>{{Clarify|date=September 2025|reason=Reference text need checking by a French speaker }} a very low number shared only with the unrelated ''[[Haplopappus gracilis]]''.{{cn|date=September 2025}}\n\n==References==\n{{reflist}}\n\n{{Taxonbar|from=Q33958333}}\n\n[[Category:Bangiophyceae]]\n\n{{Improve categories|date=September 2025}}\n\n{{Rhodophyta-stub}}",
